{"tool_name":"locusexplorer","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"locusexplorer","home":"https://github.com/oncogenetics/LocusExplorer","license":"MIT","summary":"A data visualization and exploration tool for genetic association data.","addition_date":"2018-04-22T11:01:22Z","last_update_date":"2018-12-11T19:08:59Z","tool_type":["Library"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:locusexplorer","credit":[{"email":"tokhir.dadaev@icr.ac.uk","name":"Tokhir Dadaev","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"https://github.com/oncogenetics/LocusExplorer"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Expression data visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0571"}]}],"name":"LocusExplorer","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"d.gabrielaitis","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/bioinformatics/btv690","metadata":{"abstract":"\u00a9 2015 The Author 2015. Published by Oxford University Press.Summary: In this article, we present LocusExplorer, a data visualization and exploration tool for genetic association data. LocusExplorer is written in R using the Shiny library, providing access to powerful R-based functions through a simple user interface. LocusExplorer allows users to simultaneously display genetic, statistical and biological data for humans in a single image and allows dynamic zooming and customization of the plot features. Publication quality plots may then be produced in a variety of file formats. Availability and implementation: LocusExplorer is open source and runs through R and a web browser. It is available at www.oncogenetics.icr.ac.uk/LocusExplorer/ or can be installed locally and the source code accessed from https://github.com/oncogenetics/LocusExplorer. Contact:","authors":[{"name":"Dadaev T."},{"name":"Eeles R."},{"name":"Kote-Jarai Z."},{"name":"Leongamornlert D.A."},{"name":"Saunders E.J."}],"citationCount":9,"date":"